+// only paint the prepaint cushion ahead of it (cover rect beyond the visible rect)
+// at low resolution. The leading edge you actually look at as it scrolls in stays
+// crisp; only the cushion you'd reach by continuing to fling is cheap. (During a very
+// fast fling a cushion tile can still reach the viewport before settling -- it then
+// sharpens at rest.) WEBKIT_LOWRES_VIEWPORT_FULL=1 enables it; default off = uniform
+// low-res across the whole exposed band.
+static bool lowResKeepViewportFullRes()
+{
+    static bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* env = getenv("WEBKIT_LOWRES_VIEWPORT_FULL");
